<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ardashir I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/224">224</a>–242 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ardashir I was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. Rising from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a>, he defeated the last Parthian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artabanus-iv">Artabanus IV</a> in 224 CE and was crowned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/negus-nagast">king of kings</a>. His victory ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a> and established a dynasty that ruled Iran for over four centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ardashir-i.jpg" alt="Ardashir I" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dinar_of_Ardashir_I_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
